# Secrets never enter the repo. `.env.example` is the one that ships: it names the
# variables and holds no values. Anything a provider or a tool writes a key into is
# here by shape, not by name, so a new one is covered without anyone remembering.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.dev.vars
.npmrc
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials.json
secrets.json
